Young Dolph didn't miss a beat responding to an attack on his life earlier this year with an unrelenting barrage of bangers titled Bulletproof. Today, Dolph will clear up hazy details with "KING," a documentary presented by WorldStarHipHop. "KING" follows the hounds of the stunning visual for "I'm So Real." Directed by We Hard Productions, the dreamlike visual follows Young Dolph as he dodges snakes through a lakeside forest. With "I'm So Real," Young Dolph takes yet another victory lap in his parade around the hip-hop game.

A prolific chronicler of trap tales, Dolph dropped a string of quality visuals from his recent Bulletproof project, the Kevlar-coated follow up to his Gelato mixtape. Recently, he made dead presidents fly "In Charlotte," jammed with his hood and played with bullets in "100 Shots," and stunted on his haters with Gucci Mane in "That's How I Feel." With a singular feature from Gucci Mane, Bulletproof, the latest victory march from Young Dolph is available now for stream and purchase.
